course: dictionary
lesson: 9539
title: Stole, the past of steal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Someone stole my bike.» Stole is the past tense of steal. It tells us that in the past, a person took something that was not theirs, without asking.
explain: Stole can also be a noun: a stole is a long scarf or shawl worn around the shoulders. To tell which one it is, look at the words around it. If it is about taking something, it is the verb. If someone is wearing it, it is the noun.
explain: Stole also works in phrases. «Her song stole the show» means it was the best part of the concert, and nothing was taken. «She stole a glance» means she looked quickly and secretly. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Steal is the present tense. Stole is the past tense.
fact: «Stole» (verb) means took something that was not yours, without asking.
fact: A «stole» (noun) is a long scarf or shawl worn around the shoulders.
fact: «Stole the show» means was the best part of a performance.
fact: «Stole a glance» means looked quickly and secretly. «Nicked» is a slang word that also means stole, as in «When Leah's dad was a boy he nicked sweets from Mr Patel's shop».
exercise: «Someone stole my bike.» What does stole mean? | Gave something away to a friend | *Took something that was not theirs without asking | Found something lost in the park | Bought something new in a shop
exercise: «Her song stole the show at the school concert.» What does stole the show mean? | Took the lights away from the stage | Made the audience leave early | *Was the best part of the performance | Ran off with the microphone
exercise: «She wore a long stole around her shoulders on the cold night.» What is a stole here? | A small bag for coins | *A long scarf or shawl | A kind of shoe | Someone who steals things
test: «He stole a glance at the clock.» What does stole a glance mean? | Stared at the clock for an hour | Broke the clock | *Looked quickly and secretly | Took the clock home
test: Leah's dad «nicked (stole) sweets». What does nicked mean here? | Counted | Sold | Gave | *Stole
exam: Which is the past tense of steal? | *Stole | Stealer | Steal | Stealing
